===
# Complex Nested Example

:::: {.columns; background: 'linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%)'; color: 'white'; padding: '30px'; border-radius: '15px'}
::: {.column; width: '50%'}
### Left Side
This demonstrates:
- Nested columns
- Gradient background
- Custom styling
- Full abstraction support
:::

::: {.column; width: '50%'}
### Right Side
All features work together:
1. Classes (`.columns`, `.column`)
2. Inline styles
3. Background gradients
4. Border radius
:::
::::

===
# Columns + All Abstractions

:::: {.columns; rotate: -1; scale: 1.05; transparency: 10; background: '#34495e'; color: 'white'; padding: '25px'}
::: {.column; width: '50%'; border-right: '2px solid white'; padding-right: '20px'}
### Transform Demo
Container has:
- Rotation (-1deg)
- Scale (1.05)
- Transparency (10%)
:::

::: {.column; width: '50%'; padding-left: '20px'}
### Full Power
This showcases the complete abstraction system working with Reveal.js columns!
:::
::::

===
# Practical Use Case: Before/After

:::: {.columns}
::: {.column; width: '50%'; background: '#e74c3c'; color: 'white'; padding: '20px'}
### Before
- Manual grid setup
- Complex CSS
- Hard to read
- Error-prone
:::

::: {.column; width: '50%'; background: '#2ecc71'; color: 'white'; padding: '20px'}
### After
- Simple `:::: {.columns}`
- Clean syntax
- Easy to understand
- Maintainable
:::
::::

===
# End

The `::::` delimiter enables:
- Standard Reveal.js column layouts
- Nested structure support
- Full compatibility with abstractions
- Clean, readable syntax
